m-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: bash]\nDelegating the search test investigation to a subagent while I handle the rest.\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: task]\n[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: todowrite]\nThe whole suite now passes: `python3 -m unittest` ran 16 tests with no failures. Before, it showed 15 because the broken search test file counted as a single error until it could load. I didn't change any tests.\n\nI tracked the work in the todo list and handed `tests/test_search.py` to a subagent. All fixes are in `catalog/`:\n\n- **`search.py`** (fixed by the subagent): it imported `normalize` from a module that doesn't exist, `catalog.nonexistent`. It now imports it from `catalog.text`, which already had the right function.\n- **`books.py`**: `parse_book` left the year as a string, so `age()` failed when it subtracted. The year is now converted to an `int`.\n- **`factory.py`**: `sample_books()` was missing `Emma`, which its own docstring lists. I added `Book(\"Emma\", \"Austen\", 1815, 1)`; the tests only check the title, so the author, year and copy count are my choice.\n- **`fees.py`**: the fee was days late *plus* the daily rate. It's now days late *times* the daily rate (0.25 per day).\n- **`inventory.py`**: `recent(n)` returned one event too many. It now slices `[-n:]`, and returns an empty list when `n <= 0` so that `[-0:]` doesn't return the whole history.\n- **`members.py`**: `MAX_BORROWED` was 3, but the comment above it and the tests say members can hold 5 books. It's now 5.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 4, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled":